ays remember that he is but a feeble mortal. (Calmet)"],["haydock",2,null,"haydock","Spirit of prophecy; (St. Jerome; Tirinus) or, I revived, and took courage."],["haydock",3,null,"haydock","Israel. His commission was chiefly to them. (Calmet)"],["haydock",5,null,"haydock","Forbear to sin. (Haydock) — He thus insinuates free-will. (St. Jerome) — If they refuse to hear my prophet, they will at least perceive that they are inexcusable. (Calmet)"],["haydock",6,null,"haydock","Scorpions. This people is no less destructive (Haydock) and hardened, Psalm cxvii. 12. — For might be better rendered, “though.” (Calmet)"],["haydock",8,null,"jerome","Eat. “If we do not eat the open book, we cannot teach.” (St. Jerome)"],["haydock",9,null,"haydock","Without. This was only done when the work was long. (Calmet) —"]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"],"jerome":["Jerome",1,1,420,"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/#jerome"]}}